SKILL add-requirement  v1
Add a new requirement and prove it, without weakening any existing evidence.

1. Write the requirement in spec/spec.req as: REQ-NNN | text with a measurable number | tiers
   It must contain a number (a limit, a time, a tolerance). "Works well" is rejected by G0.
2. Add at least one vector in vectors/ with "REQ REQ-NNN" and an ASSERT that checks the number.
3. Add a boundary vector: test exactly at the limit (for example sensor_stuck at the threshold).
4. Check every value is inside limits.cfg (G14). If the board limit is too tight, ask the
   hardware owner; only they can re-sign limits.cfg.
5. Run:  kindgleam check        (fast: spec, coverage, build)
6. Run:  kindgleam verify      (full chain; G7 shows whether the new test catches planted bugs)
7. Record why the requirement exists:
   kindgleam memory add decisions <source> "REQ-NNN added because ..."
